{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor","id":845442,"title":"Vampires and Body Armor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-10T21:28:58-08:00","id":845442,"title":"Vampires and Body Armor","content":"Let's talk about body armor. I heard some talk a while back about people preferring their vampires in cocktail dresses and tuxedos over riot gear and flak jackets, saying it didn't really fit the mood. I can see where they're coming from, but on the other hand armor really is pretty handy to have around. It isn't even that expensive in many parts of the world, certainly nothing that your average vampire couldn't manage.<br /> <br /> Now, let's put aside the Legion of the Dead back in medieval and Imperial Roman times, Sanctified going around wearing lorica, and the occasional Invictus knight in ceremonial armor at a formal event.<br /> <br /> Do vampires in your games typically go around using body armor? A ballistic vest under your coat? Heavy biker leathers? Heavier stuff, still? Not just your player characters who want to get an edge, but your NPCs too? <br /> <br /> In my own game I saw, at most, one of the older vampire PCs wear a coat with some kevlar plating sewn in - because he wanted to supplement his Resilience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:36:58-08:00","id":845448,"title":"","content":"I've made lots of characters that wear armor. Leathers and other reinforced clothing are common, especially among the more rough-around-the-edges types and can be passed off as punk, goth, or grunge fashion. Lots of Sheriffs will wear Kevlar vests under their clothing. Some especially paranoid characters might go full riot gear and use Obfuscate so it doesn't look out of place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T22:43:36-08:00","id":845480,"title":"","content":"It's mostly just player characters who want to get an edge, and Invictus and Sanctified who want to deliver a formal message while murdering people. And the occasional Belial's Brood, PCs love that. And Sheriffs, yeah. And Gangrel who have some kind of relevant mutation, that's popular, we go with 2/1 at Protean 2 and 4/4 if it's your Protean 4 choice. Major antagonist for a short playtesting arc was a Gangrel Crone who used the Primal Creation Cruac style for all kinds of hijinks, and the final encounter involved her as a truck-sized Kodiak bear covered in chitinous armor plating. One of four times a rocket launcher has seen actual acquisition and use at the table.<br /> <br /> Basically yes, for the simple reason that it's a really effective combat mechanic, although I wouldn't say it's common so much as just PRESENT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T04:33:30-08:00","id":845558,"title":"","content":"Yeah, wear it when you expect combat. Charity party event? Nah. &quot;Let's smash up Invictus property&quot; Carthian party? Hell yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T04:54:47-08:00","id":845559,"title":"","content":"Armor... depends a lot on the character. I would fully expect an Invictus Knight to come in armor. Whereas I expect someone trying to appear as a social butterfly to not. Vampire is, above all else, a Social game. The main struggles are going to be social before physical. So, when we come to Elysium looking to make an impression, I expect to see vampires prioritizing what impression they want to make. The knight is going to want to project the image of a guard prepared for shit to hit the fan. The socialite is going to come in outfits that provide social bonuses. Each wears clothes that make the most impact for what they're trying to accomplish.<br /> <br /> And here's the thing. Most modern armors are designed with the idea of saving you from bullets. Vampires are already bullet resistant, so that already cuts a large chunk of worry off. Armor can be big, bulky, and obvious. With Vigor in the equation, and how weapons deal auto-damage equal to their equipment modifier, you'll want to focus on just getting one success and let the auto-damage modifiers take care of the bulk of it. Claws of the Unholy shred armor like butter with a hot knife, and the social powers are both effective for putting an end to combat and not taking armor into account. Biting deals lethal to vampires, and most armor doesn't protect the neck - its worthless against such a common tactic. So, the actual benefits of mundane armor for the average vampire is actually lower than you'd think.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that armor doesn't have its uses. Armor does provide an edge in combat, and if you're expecting a fight, every little bit helped. Reinforced clothing is a general 1/0 armor that's widely applicable and pretty cheap - its an easy to get, covers most of your body, and doesn't restrict movement. So, why not wear it if you don't need the social bonuses from other clothes? Against an opponent trying to stake you, that armor can mean the difference between unlife and torpor.<br /> <br /> To me, vampires are ultimately practical. They don't eschew armor because it doesn't fit the theme. They eschew armor because while violence is part of their lives, their image is generally more important. Is it more advantagous to show up in armor and expecting a fight, or show up in an outfit that gives you an edge socially? In Elysium, physical violence is banned, so most Kindred likely won't come prepared for a fight. They'll come prepared for a social conflict. Meanwhile, the Sheriff and her Hounds are expected to come prepared for physical trouble all the time, so them NOT wearing armor is more of a cause for eyebrows being raised, imho. Going out to expect a fight? Wear the armor.<br /> <br /> Its all simply a matter of priorities. As the Social game, vampires tend to prioritize social advantages. But its not absolute. That is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T04:54:51-08:00","id":845560,"title":"","content":"Not counting special abilities that grant armor, with vampires I think I've only had armor worn by two particularly paranoid characters and only on certain occasions. Even outside of vampires there was just one werewolf who was afraid of silver bullets who wore kevlar, and a Task Force Valkyrie team that had to wear armor out on missions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:08:28-08:00","id":845583,"title":"","content":"I'm one that doesn't like vampires wearing armor in a modern setting. More savvy players tend to see the advantages of armor and pick up the item since the benefits almost always outweigh the negatives without some ST fiat. Newer players wouldn't go right to kevlar. I hate the escalation of armor, as well. Either having to give all the NPCs the same thing because every PC has it, or in PvP situations where it just seemed like a noob tax if you didn't have it.<br /> <br /> For my peace of mind and story visuals, we ended up houseruling a new inherent ability for all Kindred - blood armor. Spend 1 Vitae for a scene, and get the benefits of Kevlar. Doesn't stack with other armor equipment or powers. Players still get the bonus, I don't have to deal with a swat team every scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:27:54-08:00","id":845592,"title":"","content":"In my last game two vampires ended up fighting and grappling, and one of them was just unloading on the other with a gun at close range while the other, who had much combat dice, was just biting and sucking.<br /> <br /> I could believe vampires neurotic about order would wear armor, providing they were going out to a fight. If you know how much blood you take and don't want to take any more it's an easy way to avoid minor brush ups. Also vampires that might have a public face or are just overly concerned with their own appearance or Masquerade, and don't want to be seen with bruises and bullet holes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:35:35-08:00","id":845596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor?p=845583#post845583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my peace of mind and story visuals, we ended up houseruling a new inherent ability for all Kindred - blood armor. Spend 1 Vitae for a scene, and get the benefits of Kevlar. Doesn't stack with other armor equipment or powers. Players still get the bonus, I don't have to deal with a swat team every scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what resilience is for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:38:41-08:00","id":845599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor?p=845596#post845596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that what resilience is for?</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. However, barring a few devotions, you can't hand out Resilience to your friends.<br /> <br /> e: Basically, it's a compromise. If they were going to suit up at every even potentially dangerous situation no matter what, making it an inherent ability just saves time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:43:21-08:00","id":845602,"title":"","content":"SWAT team thing is awesome if you are expecting to fight. You usually don't (or don't want to look like you do). For normal fights, you pretty much can take care of wounds with blood healing, and armor will probably be excessive (the amount of damage it would save you would probably not end the fight anyway). Armor is important for people who are expecting to fight more than that, as it saves *tons* of blood if you are, dunno, engaging in gang warfare. But for normal, once-in-two-nights barroom brawl vampire unlife? You probably get more mileage out of +social clothes, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:49:01-08:00","id":845607,"title":"","content":"Can't beat a vamp going oldschool with full plate armour and a sword though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:50:09-08:00","id":845608,"title":"","content":"Sure you can, just get a lot of vigor and punch them really hard.<br /> I'll excuse myself.<br /> EDIT<br /> Seriously though, Kindred Fighting Style...if your opponent is using it (and I imagine that most of Sherrifs will), you will cry about not having your armor on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T08:27:00-08:00","id":845653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor?p=845583#post845583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm one that doesn't like vampires wearing armor in a modern setting. More savvy players tend to see the advantages of armor and pick up the item since the benefits almost always outweigh the negatives without some ST fiat. Newer players wouldn't go right to kevlar. I hate the escalation of armor, as well. Either having to give all the NPCs the same thing because every PC has it, or in PvP situations where it just seemed like a noob tax if you didn't have it.</div> </div> </div> </div> So... your players never thought it was a good idea to wear a nice dress or suit to impress the elder they need to meet? Get mocked by the Harpies for showing up everywhere in armor? Opponents never make head or arm shots? Use Dominate or Nightmare to just shut the PCs down? Grapple and bites? <br /> <br /> I don't want to make judgements about a group, but is it possible that the players have a combat-first mindset? It might help if you made a point to use tactics that got around armor, or just discourage combat as the best solution? CofD combat is supposed to be about violence that leaves you in pain and messed up. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T10:23:32-08:00","id":845704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor?p=845653#post845653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So... your players never thought it was a good idea to wear a nice dress or suit to impress the elder they need to meet? Get mocked by the Harpies for showing up everywhere in armor? Opponents never make head or arm shots? Use Dominate or Nightmare to just shut the PCs down? Grapple and bites?<br /> <br /> I don't want to make judgements about a group, but is it possible that the players have a combat-first mindset? It might help if you made a point to use tactics that got around armor, or just discourage combat as the best solution? CofD combat is supposed to be about violence that leaves you in pain and messed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi again, MCN!<br /> <br /> Depends on the group. My current crew has actually been pretty good about it so far under the 2E rules. In my PvP focused and 1E LARP games, it was very rampant. It wouldn't be on 24-7, and not all conflicts are resolved with combat, but any time combat was a concern, possibility or a desire, why not suit up?<br /> <br /> Also, all your suggestions make sense , but in the end they're directly player-antagonistic. Unless it's specifically adding to the dramatic story-arc, dumping on the players for buying legal equipment from the book just feels like a punishment for balance or theme's sake. But I still empathize with the thought referenced by the OP regarding SWAT teams feeling out of place or too common. I'd just prefer my house rule over your ideas unless it really drives the story forward in a meaningful way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:03:13-08:00","id":845726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor?p=845704#post845704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, all your suggestions make sense , but in the end they're directly player-antagonistic. Unless it's specifically adding to the dramatic story-arc, dumping on the players for buying legal equipment from the book just feels like a punishment for balance or theme's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they might seem player antagonistic from your point of view, but to be honest? I think its less player antagonistic and more that vampires don't fight fair. To me, the proposed suggestions are how I have my enemies fight in the first place. If I have an NPC with Dominate, Nightmare, or Obfuscate, I will use it in combat. I use grapple-biters and vampires who specializing in staking. PCs aren't the only ones allowed to fight dirty or take advantage of weaknesses. There are Gangrel running around with vicious claws that rend through steel doors like a hot knife through butter.<br /> <br /> That's not player antagonistic. That's using what I consider standard vampire tactics. Vampires specialize in controls. That's physical controls, controlling the distance of a fight, mind controls. And each is a valid tactic for both PC and NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:05:42-08:00","id":845728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor?p=845704#post845704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the group. My current crew has actually been pretty good about it so far under the 2E rules. In my PvP focused and 1E LARP games, it was very rampant. It wouldn't be on 24-7, and not all conflicts are resolved with combat, but any time combat was a concern, possibility or a desire, why not suit up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something about Requiem LARP seems to bring out the power gamer in people. Probably the fact that LARP tends to have more PvP than tabletop. In my LARP group the &quot;I'm wearing full riot gear and using Obfuscate to hide it&quot; technique was quite popular. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor?p=845704#post845704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, all your suggestions make sense , but in the end they're directly player-antagonistic. Unless it's specifically adding to the dramatic story-arc, dumping on the players for buying legal equipment from the book just feels like a punishment for balance or theme's sake. But I still empathize with the thought referenced by the OP regarding SWAT teams feeling out of place or too common. I'd just prefer my house rule over your ideas unless it really drives the story forward in a meaningful way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call MCN's suggestions player-antagonistic. Head, arm, and leg shots are a built-in weakness of bulletproof vests, both in the system and in reality. It just makes sense for opponents to target unarmored areas. Black tie events where you'd be ridiculed for wearing armor are just a fact of (un)life. It's not a punishment for power gaming, it's a natural consequence of coming to a party wearing Kevlar when everyone else is wearing Armani. Mental Disciplines like Dominate and Nightmare are standard vampire fare. It's not player-antagonistic to have NPCs use their abilities, it's just playing the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:25:19-08:00","id":845738,"title":"","content":"Instead of making armor less attractive, you can always make non-armor more attractive. Better impressions, social dice bonuses (hey, a cute dress can be like having 1 more dot in all social skills, you know), some non quantifiable benefits...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:27:32-08:00","id":845741,"title":"","content":"Called shots are fine and are basically a trade-off benefit to the character for either less damage or more defense, in both cases better to have armor than not. Standard vampire fair is also fine, not every conflict has to be about combat and I'm familiar with how to take into account tactics, strengths and weaknesses of my players when setting up such head-to-heads, judgments about my group aside.<br /> <br /> Forcing various social or other consequences on the player characters <i>specifically </i>to address a thematic/escalation issue (armor) does feel player-antagonistic to me. As always, the best way to address it is to just discuss it at the table directly. For games where that isn't as possible (pickup games, LARP, etc), I like my compromise. Keeps the benefit of armor for those who want it, keeps the set dressing away from the SWAT theme. YMMV, of course, and thanks for the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:47:46-08:00","id":845750,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, setting up those situations specifically to address a perceived overuse of armor by players is antagonistic. But formal events are a thing that should be happening regardless of whether characters wear armor. Formal events are just part of vampire like tavern scenes are a part of D&amp;D. And if players wear armor to such events, they're likely to run into problems. I do agree though that talking to the players is always the best solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T12:08:27-08:00","id":845759,"title":"","content":"Vampires are probably better at social pressure than high schoolers. Going to a formal event in armor would probably be like going to the prom in, well, armor. You could only pull it off if you're exceptionally cool or it's what people expect from you, like you're a knight or something. Otherwise for the rest of your unlife they'll call you Tankula and Iron Mekhet. Juggernoss? Circle of Chrome?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Bulletproof Vent? 03-11-2016, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T12:22:11-08:00","id":845767,"title":"","content":"I just popped into the thread and was treated to the image of a formal event populated solely by vampires in full riot gear using obsfucate to draw attention away from it, and the nickname 'Tankula.'<br /> <br /> Y'all have made my Friday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T14:03:58-08:00","id":845823,"title":"","content":"Allow players &quot;called shots&quot; on Social rolls. Usually, a nice clothing will be enough to offset the &quot;called shot&quot; penalty and will be seen as attractive option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T15:13:21-08:00","id":845842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor?p=845823#post845823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allow players &quot;called shots&quot; on Social rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T17:06:04-08:00","id":845885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor?p=845842#post845842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I resolve a lot of social rolls that are not manuevering or contested (I don't like contested rolls that much honestly, too much time consuming and often too random) using following method:<br /> A simple roll of Skill+Attribute+Equipment, with penalties:<br /> -1 for each dot in appropiate Resistance Attribute (it's easy to come up with Res Attribute even if you literally don't have the NPC statted up)<br /> -1 for 1st, 3rd and 5th dots of appropiate &quot;counter&quot; Skill (so if you try to lie to someone with Subterfuge 3, they will reduce your pool by 2)<br /> - &quot;called shot&quot; penalty to achieve whatever flamboyant result you want. <br /> - circumstancial penalties that often are similar to &quot;when to increase number of doors by x&quot;<br /> <br /> This way, it works a lot like combat; you want to have around 3-4 dice left in your pool to have a good shot at your social roll, and utilize any leftovers for weaving in cool effects. It also allows me to reward social specialists with more interesting tools, and gate certain results behind relatively big penalties that will usually put you at chance dice at best. This way, when a player gets +2 to social roll from their clothes, they can actively use it to declare something like &quot;I want to impress him!&quot;, and because it might be -2 to do so, clothes feel like they are &quot;directly&quot; responsible for doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T09:13:23-07:00","id":848217,"title":"","content":"Or, you could go fancy AND bulletproof. Seriously, google &quot;bulletproof clothing&quot;. I imagine you can't go riot armor level of protection like that, but I bet you can get flak jacket level for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/290-blackyce","name":"blackyce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T07:04:56-07:00","id":852396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor?p=845750#post845750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yeah, setting up those situations specifically to address a perceived overuse of armor by players is antagonistic. But formal events are a thing that should be happening regardless of whether characters wear armor. Formal events are just part of vampire like tavern scenes are a part of D&amp;D. And if players wear armor to such events, they're likely to run into problems. I do agree though that talking to the players is always the best solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>To drive the point home: what if someone showed up to SWAT-raid level combat situation in a tuxedo? At best they'd be ridiculed, at worst completely barred from participating until they changed into something more appropriate and started treating the situation with the seriousness it deserves.<br /> <br /> Same reasoning behind showing up to a social event in a kevlar vest. People are at best going to snark at you, at worst you'll be told you're not allowed in until you change to conform with the dress code. No shirt, no shoes, no service.<br /> <br /> My game only had one character who routinely wore armor, and that was the police officer Geist who'd been killed by her own service weapon (so her never forgetting to wear her vest again made perfect sense.) Then again, the crossover group also included an Obrimos Mage who handed out Mage Armor like it was going out of style, and Bound had the Shroud Manifestation as well. But basically, mundane armor pales in comparison to the kinds of armor supernaturals can get. Vampires are intrinsically pretty damage-resistant, and loading Resilience on top of that generally means kevlar is a less-attractive option. Also, the main draw of bulletproof armors is the reduction of gunshot wounds to bashing damage, something vampires have just by virtue of being vampires (and better than a bulletproof armor does, if memory serves.) The reduction of damage tends to be minimal, again if memory serves. It could certainly save your unlife in a heavy combat situation, but in most situations it's probably not worth it, except for those wanting to squeeze every last ounce of efficiency out of their character builds. I'm not saying &quot;armor's only for munchkins,&quot; just that there are probably better investments for those Resources dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T07:25:17-07:00","id":852415,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Kevlar Vests have torso coverage, reduce all incoming damage by 1 and downgrade the first 3 points of damage from firearms attacks to bashing. Since vampires already downgrade damage from mundane weapons to bashing, the only actual benefit they get is the 1 point of soak. Reinforced Clothing has the exact same benefit for vampires, extends the coverage to arms and legs, and can be more easily passed off as fashion. It's just straight up a better option. Other armors provide better general armor, but are more conspicuous. Generally, a vampire's natural resistance to mundane weapons, Vitae healing, and Resilience will be more than enough to protect them. Armor is really more of a fashion statement for vampires than actual protection. And the statement that is made by going around with unnecessary amounts of armor in everyday situations is not one most vampires will think highly of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T15:33:44-07:00","id":854230,"title":"","content":"As someone pointed out above, no need to sacrifice style for protection. <a href=\"http://garrisonbespoke.com/custom-suits/bulletproof-suit/\" target=\"_blank\">http://garrisonbespoke.com/custom-su...letproof-suit/</a><br /> That shop is a pretty well known place out of Toronto. If you watch Hannibal or Suits on USA, they do the men's clothing. So, any Daeva or Ventrue could still have a status symbol while having added protection as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T03:36:21-07:00","id":854968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merinoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor?p=854230#post854230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone pointed out above, no need to sacrifice style for protection. <a href=\"http://garrisonbespoke.com/custom-suits/bulletproof-suit/\" target=\"_blank\">http://garrisonbespoke.com/custom-su...letproof-suit/</a><br /> That shop is a pretty well known place out of Toronto. If you watch Hannibal or Suits on USA, they do the men's clothing. So, any Daeva or Ventrue could still have a status symbol while having added protection as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 20k dollars. Not something everyone can easily shell out. However, those with the financial capabilities (and vampires have plenty of time to get those up and running), certainly do. So.. those elysiums with all fancy dresses and shit? Could be armor. <br /> <br /> Anyways, how does that armor pair up against swords and blades and things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T04:39:01-07:00","id":854991,"title":"","content":"I can see Invictus handing those out for free as a PR stunt, show of power and Masquerade fortification.<br /> Happy Embrace, congrats on starting your Requiem! Here is your Embrace gift, ridiculously expensive but practical suit with a invictus logo somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T06:53:31-07:00","id":855050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/845442-vampires-and-body-armor?p=854991#post854991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see Invictus handing those out for free as a PR stunt, show of power and Masquerade fortification.<br /> Happy Embrace, congrats on starting your Requiem! Here is your Embrace gift, ridiculously expensive but practical suit with a invictus logo somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'm now having a nasty idea about retooling The Kingsmen as an Invictus entity. Elite, gentlemen spy enforcers in bulletproof suits with fascinating spy gadgets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}